C. BUREAU OF FIELD OPERATIONS 2
C - 1. Command and Control
The Bureau of Field Operations 2 (East) is commanded by a Deputy Chief of
Police, whose primary responsibility is to provide general management
direction and control for the Bureau.
C - 2. Incorporated Units
The Bureau of Field Operations 2 consists of:
1. Patrol Area 4;
2. Patrol Area 5;
3. Patrol Area 6; and
4. Support Operations Division.
D. BUREAU OF INVESTIGATIONS
D - 1. Command and Control
The Bureau of Investigations is commanded by a Deputy Chief of Police,
whose primary responsibility is to provide general management direction and
control for the Bureau.
D - 2. Incorporated Units
The Bureau of Investigations consists of:
1. Criminal Investigation Division;
• Homicide Section;
• Robbery & Felony Assault Section;
• Special Victims Section; Youth Service, Domestic Violence, Child
Exploitation & Missing Persons;
• Burglary, General Crimes, Field Support, & Evidence;
2. Violent Crime Operations Center;
• Crime Gun Intelligence Center;
• Intelligence Unit;
• Gun E-Trace Unit;
3. Criminalistics Division; and
4. Crime Analysis Section.

